From 10a32cc5e60efee3b51f75a4bb5affcc3b8efb70 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 09:51:25 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Launcher: mGBA options off by default, GB-Link collapsible,
 FRLG/RS saves rebuild into Emerald

The mGBA emulation section starts closed with "GBA as controller" and
"Mirror GBA screen" off. The GB-Link section folds away like it and starts
open with "Real GBA" on. The netplay lag test option is gone; the lag model
still runs in netplay.

A FireRed/LeafGreen or Ruby/Sapphire save picked for an Emerald port (or read
whole from a cartridge) was refused as a mismatch. Its party and trainer are
now copied into an Emerald save, like a team-only cartridge read, and the
trainer keeps the cartridge's look in battle.
